  "result": "The bug is an off-by-one error and it's fixed. All 6 tests now pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD`, where the threshold is 10. A line of exactly 10 units therefore didn't qualify, so the discount only started at 11 units.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the check to `>=`, so the discount now applies at 10 or more units as the policy says:\n\n```python\nif line.qty >= BULK_THRESHOLD:\n```\n\n**Tests:** `python3 -m unittest discover`: 6 passed, 0 failed. The existing `test_bulk_discount` covers this exact case: 10 units at $1.00 should total $10.28 (the $10.00 subtotal minus the 5% discount, plus 8.25% tax). The old code would have given $10.83. I didn't run the tests before making the change, though, so I haven't confirmed that this test was failing beforehand.\n\nThere's no test yet for 9 units, the case just below the threshold. One would catch the comparison being wrong in the other direction. I can add it if you'd like.",
